  "beruf": "kraftfahrer",
  "title": "Driving and delivery",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "spanish-for-work run, 2026-11-07: written by hand for Spain, read once by an AI second reader, not yet by a human. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation (the 'German' tab). Words already in the lexicon or in another deck are refs, with this job's own example and sense. Working conditions are general orientation only.",
  "intro": "Delivering parcels, food and goods (reparto) is a common job in Spanish cities, by van, motorbike or lorry. This deck has the vehicle, your daily work, routes and deliveries, the rules and safety, and what you say at the door. For the driving test itself, see the DGT vocabulary.",
  "introEasy": "Do you deliver parcels or food, or drive for work in Spain? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Repartidor/a",
    "Conductor/a de furgoneta",
    "Camionero/a",
    "Mensajero/a",
    "Rider"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "At the door, one short sentence is enough: «Buenos días, un paquete para Ana García. ¿Me firma aquí?»",
    "Through the entryphone, say who you are and what you bring: «Hola, es el repartidor. Traigo un paquete.»",
    "Foreign licences are not always valid for long, and professional driving needs extra permits. Check with the DGT or your employer before you drive for work. This is general orientation, not legal advice."
  ],
